WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.940
How can a falling phone have a speed at one single instant?

00:00:03.940 --> 00:00:07.660
Speed is distance over time. That needs two moments.

00:00:07.660 --> 00:00:12.310
From 2 to 3 seconds: 24.5 metres per second.

00:00:12.310 --> 00:00:16.370
Shrink the gap to 2.1: 20.09.

00:00:16.370 --> 00:00:21.950
2.01: 19.649. The answers start to settle.

00:00:21.950 --> 00:00:28.010
They close in on 19.6. That is the speed at exactly 2 seconds.
